Description: xcb: read input device names using their length
 xcb_input_xi_device_info_name() returns a pointer into the QueryDevice
 reply; the name is not NUL-terminated but exactly name_length bytes long.
 The master keyboard, master pointer and slave keyboard paths pass that
 pointer to QString::fromUtf8() as a C string, so the conversion reads past
 the end of the name. On a stock Xorg or Xvfb this affects every session:
 "Virtual core pointer" is 20 bytes, so the reply has no zero padding and
 the byte after the name is the first device class (XIButtonClass = 1);
 QInputDevice::name() returns "Virtual core pointer\x01".
 .
 Pass xcb_input_xi_device_info_name_length() to the conversion, as the
 tablet and touch paths already do.
 .
 tst_qinputdevice checks on xcb that no device name contains a control
 character.
Author: JiDe Zhang <zhangjide@uniontech.com>
Origin: backport, https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtbase/+/791786
Applied-Upstream: commit:39ca1160c1c9a934d5c5ae8326c1ff91a21425e4
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
---
